usage() {
    cat <<'EOF'
Usage: multifetch [OPTION]... KEYWORD...
       ... | multifetch [OPTION]...          (keywords from stdin, one per line)
Search the web and many sites for KEYWORD: a course, a release, a name.

Modes (default: pick in fzf on a terminal, --print in a pipe):
  -p, --print            every search as category<TAB>label<TAB>url
  -s, --scan             run the searches through the Brave API, save hits
  -n, --new              hits of the latest scan no earlier scan had
  -d, --discover         search the sites directly, list posts and new hosts
  -a, --add              with -d: add the hosts found to your site list
  -i, --iptv             public IPTV playlists, checked; Enter adds one to reel
  -l, --sites            every built-in site and whether it resolves
  -e, --edit             edit your extra site list

Choosing:
  -c, --category CAT     only these categories (repeat, or comma-separated);
                         -c list prints the categories
  -f, --file FILE        keywords from FILE, one per line ("-" = stdin)
  -w, --words            every word its own keyword (default: unquoted words
                         are one name; quoted arguments one keyword each)

Output:
  -u, --urls             URLs only, one per line
  -C, --count            only the number of results
  -m, --max N            stop after N results
  -j, --json             one JSON object per line
  -H, --no-header        no header line in tables
  -q, --quiet            nothing printed; the exit status says it
      --color[=WHEN]     colour: auto (default), always, never
  -o, --open             open every result in the browser, no fzf
  -h, --help             this help
  -V, --version          the version
  --                     end of options (a keyword may then start with -)

Exit status: 0 something found, 1 nothing found, 2 an error (as grep).

Examples:
  multifetch "Course Name" "Creator"            pick in fzf, open in the browser
  multifetch -p -c torrent,file-host Name        two categories as a table
  multifetch -pu Name | xargs -n1 xdg-open      every URL into the browser
  cat names.txt | multifetch -j | jq .url        many keywords, JSON out
  multifetch -s Name && multifetch -n Name       scan, then what is new
  multifetch -i germany                          IPTV lists for Germany

Files: extra sites in ~/.config/multifetch/sites, scans in ~/.local/share/multifetch/.
--scan needs BRAVE_API_KEY in ~/.secure/apikeys (free tier: api.search.brave.com).
EOF
}

